n to the higher roof Andre  says that the trunk clearly positions  the car as a sub beam segment vehicle  less than a B but more than a mini the  cargo space is definitely enough for an  ordinary trip one little niggle when you  open the trunk there's not much to see  you could describe as cleanest as  inexpensive well they have to keep the  price down somehow check on the model we  tested came with the cool and sound  package for a sticker price of eleven  thousand six hundred euros you get a CD  audio system voice control manually  adjustable aircon and an emergency call  assistant it calls for help via a  Bluetooth connected cell phone if the  air bag inflates  [Music]  Andre says that the cob plus puts  pressure on the competition with its  price and size but Ford has also kept  the vehicle in check so that it doesn't  steal customers away from the Fiesta for  example with a relatively small  old-fashioned infotainment display panel  it's being phased out of the eighth  generation Fiesta which will have a  large touchscreen but with the Cobb plus  it's unfortunately the best you can get  the cool and sound comes automatically  with the high performance 1.2 liter  4-cylinder induction engine variant that  has 63 instead of 51 kilowatts and it's  the most powerful cop you can buy  [Music]  Oh Hungary says that in terms of the  engine that keeps a respectful distance  from his big brother the fiestas the car  does not have the latter's 3 cylinder  EcoBoost unit which one an engine of the  Year award there are also no six-speed  manual or automatic gearbox options the  engine in the car plus is adequate but  not much fun to drive the suspension is  above average for the a segment that the  engine loses points but a more tour  Deborah misters Gansett and awesome bits  in ours there are a number of a segment  cars with a lively 3-cylinder turbo  engine despite the amount of hard  plastic the interior of the car plus is  stylish and practical with four drink  holders in between the front seats plus  some extra ones in the back no one's  going to get thirsty  [Music]  the trunk lamp can be turned by pressing  a button next to the light switch or the  key  [Music]  Andre thinks that Ford should have come  up with another designation for the car  plus his segment sub B implies that the  cars been artificially kept below the  Fiesta which is a bit unfair what buyers  get is a more top a segment car at an a  segment price a vehicle that offers more  space and better handling than is  usually the case in the a segment -  forgive me sue  [Music]  an all-wheel drive crossover in Ireland  ideal terrain for the new Suzuki sx4 s  cross to show what it's capable of the  weather here seems to change by the hour  from wind and rain to blue skies our car  reviewer Michelle wants to see whether  the SX 4s cross lives up to Suzuki's  promise to get you where you're going  fast rain or shine  she's testing the version with a 1.4  liter gasoline engine delivering 103  kilowatts of power and a peak torque of  220 Newton meters  it makes the dash to 100 kilometers per  hour and a little over 10 seconds the  manufacturers fuel economy rating is 5.6  liters for 100 kilometers our Edition  has the comfort plus equipment line  prices and Germany started just under 29  thousand euros personally Michelle finds  the engine a little weak and the  steering too soft  she misses that feedback from the  driving surface  among the optional extras is the  all-wheel-drive system all grip last  year's facelift added two new engines to  choose from there's the 1 liter  3-cylinder diesel unit with 82 kilowatts  and the newest and most powerful  gasoline Edition that we're testing the  SX 4s cross does not have permanent  all-wheel drive it's primarily powered  via the front axle if it loses traction  the car switches to both axles this can  take a little more time than expected a  feeling that takes getting used to  but now it's time to unleash all grip as  we go off-